config UHC_XHCI_ALIF
	bool "Alif Ensemble xHCI USB host controller driver"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_ALIF_XHCI_UHC_ENABLED
	depends on UHC_DRIVER
	help
	  xHCI USB-2.0 host driver for the Alif Ensemble USB (DWC3-family,
	  controller base 0x48200000, IRQ 101).

	  Implements the full uhc_api: DWC3 host-mode init + xHCI reset,
	  command/event-ring processing, root-hub port reset + single-device
	  enumeration, ep_enqueue/ep_dequeue (control/bulk -- NOT interrupt;
	  an interrupt endpoint returns -ENOTSUP, since this driver's
	  ep_enqueue() is fully synchronous and a real interrupt-IN needs
	  periodic, asynchronous completion this driver does not implement),
	  bus reset/suspend/resume, disable/shutdown, and an event-ring IRQ
	  for hotplug notification.

	  Only *_enable()'s controller bring-up itself -- DWC3 host-mode
	  init, xHCI reset, and the command/event-ring round trip (No-Op +
	  Enable Slot commands) -- was proven on an E8 EVK (see the timing
	  comments in uhc_xhci_alif_first_light()); uhc_xhci_alif_enumerate()'s
	  device-dependent stages (Address Device, GET_DESCRIPTOR) did NOT
	  reach completion on that same bench session, blocked on the EVK's
	  D+/D- signal path.  Everything else (ep_enqueue/ep_dequeue, bus
	  suspend/resume, disable/shutdown, the ISR) follows the same
	  register sequencing but has NOT itself been bench-run -- see issue
	  #388 for the open bench checklist.

	  Do NOT enable this on a production build until the above has a
	  bench pass: this is a from-spec implementation with no hardware
	  confirmation past controller bring-up, on a peripheral (USB host)
	  that drives an external, untrusted device.

	  Driver: zephyr/drivers/usb/uhc/uhc_xhci_alif.c
	  Binding: zephyr/dts/bindings/usb/alif,xhci-uhc.yaml
